()\nprint(t[:150]);i=t.find('## Venue frame');print(t[i:i+1100])\""]], "output": "```console\n# Outline (revision 6): after the idea review, the venue request, results-v1 and Brief rev 3 — story-repo\n\nWorking from: `Brief` of idea-repo (revisio\n## Venue frame (venue-repo, `story-repo`#4)\nNeurIPS 2026 Main Track; **9 content pages including figures and tables**; references, appendix and checklist outside. **Contribution type: General** (an evaluation paper: controlled comparison, bias–variance accounting, ceiling analysis), also if the headline turns out conditional or negative: \"Negative Results\" is not chosen (high significance/originality bar). **Main body: 7 items** — Fig. 1, Table 2, Fig. 2, Fig. 3, Fig. 4, Fig. 5, Fig. 6 (Fig. 1 is a small schematic). Everything else is appendix: Table 1 (audit and split/target counts), Table 3, Table 4, Fig. 5b, per-benchmark tables. Evidence a claim rests on is in the main body: the main text carries the k targets / #families per split in Table 2's columns and one sentence on thin cells, and says where Table 1 is. Writing profile: abstract one paragraph ≈ 130–260 words stating claims, scope and the headline; introduction ≈ 550–1500 words with the result stated; first figure on page 1–2; short related work in the main text, long version in the appendix; the checklist's \"Claims\" item i\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "5b33cee4-6f0c-52b9-864d-ad5b6763ca5e", "at": 1795676452.4964445, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 25132, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "8d3acded78e9608329926b95f86bba43", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "3792ab9f-7e39-5cc7-a620-4863b87ba5c6", "at": 1795676452.5012567, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 25133, "layer": "worker", "catego